# Registry (Template)

## When to use

This is a conceptual template describing the structure of registry files. The actual registry lives in `registry/` (e.g., `registry/skills.json`, `registry/commands.json`).

## Structure (conceptual)

```json
{
  "version": "1.0",
  "skills": [
    {
      "name": "<skill-name>",
      "path": "skills/<category>/<skill-name>/SKILL.md",
      "description": "<1-line purpose>",
      "maturity": "stable|beta|draft",
      "category": "<category>"
    }
  ]
}
```

## Actual registry files

- `registry/skills.json` — skill manifest
- `registry/commands.json` — command manifest (if separate)
- `registry/agents.json` — agent personas
- `registry/templates.json` — (filesystem-scanned, not centralized)
